se countries do experience socio-sanitary impacts associated with chronic diarrhea, which has a higher prevalence in these regions due to various lifestyle factors.", "LACTULOSA:Lactulosa is a synthetic sugar that serves multiple purposes in health care. Primarily, it is recognized as a laxative used to treat constipation. Additionally, Lactulosa functions as a prebiotic, resisting digestion and promoting gut health. This dual role highlights its importance in both alleviating digestive issues and supporting overall gastrointestinal well-being.", "INULINA:Inulina is a type of soluble fiber that serves as a prebiotic, promoting the growth of beneficial gut bacteria. It is commonly used in dietary and nutritional products due to its health benefits and positive effects on digestive health. Inulina is recognized for its prebiotic properties, making it a valuable ingredient in various food products aimed at enhancing gut health.", "FRUCTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSACÁRIDOS:Fructooligosaccharides (FOS) are prebiotic carbohydrates that promote the growth of beneficial bacteria in the gut.", "SÍNDROME DEL INTESTINO IRRITABLE:El síndrome del intestino irritable (SIC), conocido en inglés como Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS), es una condición gastrointestinal común que puede ser influenciada por la dieta y la fermentación de alimentos. Esta afección se caracteriza por síntomas como dolor abdominal y cambios en los hábitos intestinales, que pueden incluir episodios de diarrea. El síndrome del intestino irritable es frecuentemente discutido en el contexto de la salud intestinal, lo que resalta su relevancia en el bienestar general del sistema digestivo.", "GALACTOLOSGALACTOLIGOSACÁRIDOS:", "DIARREA INVASIVA:Diarrea invasiva or dysentery is a more severe form of diarrhea where mucus or blood is present in the stool, often linked to infections by specific pathogens.", "ESCHIRICHIA COLI:Escherichia coli is a type of bacteria that can cause severe gastrointestinal illness, including diarrhea.", "ENTAMOEBA HISTOLYTICA:Entamoeba histolytica is a parasitic protozoan that can cause amoebic dysentery and is associated with diarrhea.", "VIBRIO CHOLERAE:Vibrio cholerae is a bacterium that causes cholera, leading to severe watery diarrhea and high morbidity and mortality rates.", "SALMONELLA:Salmonella is a genus of bacteria that can cause foodborne illness, often resulting in diarrhea.", "CAMPYLOBACTER:Campylobacter is a type of bacteria that can lead to gastrointestinal infections, commonly resulting in diarrhea."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}